id: pm-github-f1at
title: Fail-closed privacy gate for automated GitHub issue imports and one reusable sync workflow
description: "Automated fleet-wide sync is disabled because the pilot workflow pushes imported issue text to a public branch before any privacy gate inspects the proposed tracker diff. Add a fail-closed scanner over the proposed tracker change, wire it into import as --gate, and ship one reusable workflow_call sync workflow fleet repos can call."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:ci","area:gates","area:import","area:privacy"
created_at: "2026-10-05T06:09:58.912Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T07:00:44.735Z"
assignee: codex-sol
claim_principal: codex-sol
author: pi-glm
acceptance_criteria: A fresh checkout installs the pinned extension and exercises a nonempty issue import; malicious issue-body credential and personal-data fixtures prevent any public branch push; completeness and idempotency are checked before mutation; a clean import opens a reviewable PR with permanent PM links; existing pilot workflows and future rollouts use one audited implementation or equivalent gate.
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-05T06:21:37.672Z",pi-glm,"Design settled: new gate.ts holds the pure scanner (credential/personal-data/host-path rules over ADDED lines only, sha256 content-hash allowlist with required written justification, fail-closed on unreadable input/git failure/malformed allowlist); unified-diff parser with toon field attribution + jsonl patch-entry attribution; git collector covers staged+working+untracked under the resolved tracker path and excludes operational locks/extensions/checkpoints subpaths. Registered as 'pm github gate' (--diff, --allowlist) and composed into import via --gate: plan completeness + provenance idempotency verified pre-mutation, tracker-change scan post-write, non-zero exit so a workflow can never push on a finding. Reusable workflow_call sync workflow added with SHA-pinned actions; caller example at docs/sync-workflow-caller.yml."
  "2026-10-05T06:33:25.742Z",pi-glm,"Implementation checkpoint: gate.ts (scanner + unified-diff parser with toon/jsonl field attribution + git collector over staged/working/untracked tracker changes, operational locks/extensions/checkpoints excluded + sha256-keyed allowlist with required justification) is registered as 'pm github gate' and composed into import via --gate (plan completeness + provenance idempotency verified pre-mutation, fail-closed scan post-write, non-zero exit). Reusable workflow_call sync workflow with SHA-pinned actions + caller example added. Full package suite green: 347 tests pass, coverage 93.55 lines / 84.05 branches / 93.62 functions (repo thresholds 88/79/89 met), docstring gate 119/119, repo privacy gate clean over 3107 objects. New suites test/gate.test.ts (29) and test/import-gate.test.ts (13) include the adversarial full-sequence replay on a real git repo with a bare remote: token-in-body, token-in-comment, email, host-path, and high-entropy fixtures all fail the gated import before anything can be pushed, and the remote's ref list never gains the sync branch."
  "2026-10-05T06:42:46.064Z",codex-sol,"Resumed interrupted run as codex-sol. Preserving implementation commit and README draft. Verification priorities: scanner fail-closed inputs and redaction, full bare-remote sequence, SDK-resolved tracker paths, reusable workflow input safety and existing PR updates, real public issue acceptance, and requested all-source 100 percent coverage. Previous evidence met only the existing lower thresholds; this is not the requested coverage gate."
  "2026-10-05T06:44:15.604Z",codex-sol,"Verified inherited code with npm run typecheck, npm run docstring (119 declarations), and node --test test/gate.test.ts test/import-gate.test.ts (42 passed). Preserved README draft, removed host-path examples, and marked rollout references as release placeholders because the current published version predates the gate. Review identified staged-versus-working-tree and same-rule allowlist deduplication bypasses; fixes and regression tests follow."
  "2026-10-05T06:58:12.486Z",codex-sol,"Resumed verification found and fixed distinct-content allowlist suppression, staged-content omission, malformed/binary diff acceptance, unreadable optional allowlists, and escaped token/path parsing. Regression suite now passes 47 gate/import tests; lock tests passed in the prior focused run. Workflow now validates same-repository automated branch and exact version inputs through environment variables, imports comments, checks gate availability, verifies the second import has no filesystem changes, and uses a branch-specific force-with-lease. The inherited test commit contained a synthetic PEM header; retained exact-blob provenance documents that false positive without rewriting history."
  "2026-10-05T07:00:44.735Z",codex-sol,"Real public acceptance: a fresh scratch pm project installed pinned PM CLI 2026.10.4 and the packed pm-github candidate 2026.10.4. Read-only unbraind/pm-todos import planned 3 issues, imported 3 items, reconciled fetched/planned/skipped as 3/3/0, passed privacy scanning over 6 changed files with zero findings, and completed in 10.84 seconds. A second gated atomic import exited zero and left all tracker item/history bytes identical. No remote or push was used. Final candidate will be rerun with comments and native Bun before reporting completion."
